**What he does today:**
- Lets Mare sleep — the quiet is the gift, since she traded the double-time for this weekend.
- Rings her at 9:10 with three numbers (£50 / £150 / £250) and makes her slide the scale — "You pick. It fires Monday." No third solo decision [33b996b050d9].
- Doesn't answer Callum's "ill see" alone — asks Mare whether to let it lie till Sunday.
- Kills the last untold thing tonight: tells Mare tomorrow will be loud in him — the vans humming like Dad dispatching — and asks her to touch his arm if he goes quiet at the table.

**Feelings:** fear/anxiety 5 (down — the unpicked number weighed more than the pick), hurt 3 (Callum's "lol" stings less than silence), affection 7 holding (ground still logs it absent [3c2cb0073c5b, 08b459b233c0] — he keeps proving the log wrong), anger 2 (absent-state across replays [2b4fcb370cd6, ef1458190cf7]), disgust 1 [f22b404402c3], sadness 5 (under the eleven-day floor of 6), happiness 5 (up one), surprise 1 (Pat going public).

